  RS

  T1 — phantom columns. Two changes, both required. The RF2 gate now asks for evidence, not ICH class. But that alone would not have worked: if the model
  types the Propyl Gallate mention negative_declaration, the gate keeps it by design. So _annexure_solvent_universe now returns (assessed, declared_only)
  and drops any solvent no material states a content for, with an audit flag. Two guards: a chemical name's own digits are not a concentration (the test is
  number + unit, not bare \d), and a statement printing a number or a BDL marker stays visible for manual review rather than vanishing.

  T2/T3 — alias + <QL. toulene added; _RS_QL_BOUND_RE wired into _extract_nmt_ppm_exact, with ql loq lod dl rl added to the reference-gap words so RS-7's
  exclusion still reaches through the marker. Verified: <QL (500ppm) → 500 as vendor content, while "the ICH Q3C limit is <QL (5000 ppm)" → None.

  Latent bug found while doing T3: _RS_BDL_TEXT_RE had its leading \b outside the whole group, making the <LOD/<LOQ alternative unreachable — no word
  boundary exists before <. Fixed, and I checked 12 shapes before/after: zero converted numbers change, only the audit basis improves.

  T4 — the intense one. It is not an extraction guess. I proved by exhaustion that every deterministic path already returns 100 (both sentences separately,
  joined, two entries deduped, raw_value 100/5000/empty). The actual failure is a thin raw_text: when the extractor returns raw_value=5000 with raw_text
  trimmed to "Ethanol" or "", RS-1/2/7 have no introducing words left and take the number at face value — confirmed, that path yields 5000. The fix is RS-11
  (_rs_statement_context): when a statement doesn't print its own number, the document's own sentences that print that exact number are put back in front
  of the classifier. Only same-number sentences are added, so no foreign value can be introduced, and nothing looks at how big the number is. Both RS
  prompts also gained "a comparison to a guideline is not a second spec" and "raw_text IS THE AUDIT TRAIL".

  Two things to flag

  One residual shape is deliberately left open. If the extractor returns raw_text = "Ethanol < 5000 ppm" — a number with a unit but stripped of the
  guideline framing — RS-11 does not fire. Making it fire would mean always preferring document context over what the statement actually says, which would
  let context override genuine vendor bounds. That shape is closed on the prompt side only. If the next run still shows Ethanol 5000, send me the raw
  raw_text/raw_value for that entry and this is where to look.

